#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for the dbus interface, which lets snaps communicate over "
"D-Bus using well-known names on the system or session bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:8
msgid "dbus interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`dbus` enables ownership of a specific name on the session or system D-Bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:12
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"`name` (slot): well-known D-Bus connection name for the service (eg, "
"`org.foo.bar`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:15
msgid "`bus` (slot): D-Bus bus to use (ie, `session` or `system`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:16
msgid ""
"`name` (plug): well-known D-Bus connection name of the service from the "
"providing snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:17
msgid "`bus` (plug): D-Bus bus to use for providing snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"The `dbus` slot is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances <interfaces-"
"parallel-installs-unsupported>`. The slot owns a unique system-wide resource "
"that instances would conflict over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:23
msgid ""
"Snaps that want to communicate via a well-known D-Bus connection name need "
"to have matching `bus` and `name` attributes and then be connected via `snap "
"connect`. Snaps specifying `bus: system` will have a default D-Bus bus "
"policy that allows `root` to own the name and anyone to send to a "
"destination that matches the well-known name (eg, `org.foo.bar`). Once "
"connected, the consuming snap may communicate with the providing snap via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:25
msgid "the specified well-known D-Bus connection name (eg, `org.foo.bar`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"a unique D-Bus connection name using a matching D-Bus interface  (eg, "
"`org.foo.bar.baz`) or D-Bus path (eg, `/org/foo/bar/norf`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"This interface is particularly well-suited for leaf-style applications from "
"GNOME, KDE, etc to integrate into the desktop session. Future versions of "
"snapd may allow greater flexibility for bus policy, D-Bus interfaces and D-"
"Bus paths and also support session services and D-Bus activation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:31
msgid ""
"Note: when developing snaps using devmode for D-Bus system services, the "
"slot implementation must use this interface so that snapd may adjust the D-"
"Bus bus policy so the snap may use the system bus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:34
msgid "Using the D-Bus interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:36
msgid ""
"The dbus interface provides a way for snaps to communicate over D-Bus. The "
"snap providing the D-Bus service declares a slot with the well-known D-Bus "
"name and which bus it uses. Snaps wanting to communicate with the providing "
"snap's service declare a plug for the providing snap. Note that a snap "
"declaration is needed for your snap to be delivered via the snap store and "
"claim this well-known D-Bus name (simply upload the snap to the store and "
"request a manual review and a reviewer will take a look)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:38
msgid ""
"When a providing snap is installed, snapd will generate security policy that "
"will allow it to listen on the well-known D-Bus name on the specified bus. "
"If the `system` bus is specified, snapd will also generate D-Bus bus policy "
"that allows 'root' to own the name and any user to communicate with the "
"service. Non-snap processes are allowed to communicate with the providing "
"snap following traditional permissions checks. Other (consuming) snaps may "
"only communicate with the providing snap by connecting the snaps' interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:40
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:42
msgid "Desktop application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:43
msgid ""
"Desktop applications sometimes listen on a well-known D-Bus name so that "
"other desktop session services and applications may interact with them. This "
"is common for GNOME and KDE applications, for example. Snaps listening on "
"the session bus may only be accessed by processes running in the user's "
"session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:45
msgid "Providing snap (slot)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:46
msgid ""
"As a developer, if your application listens on the `session` bus with the "
"well-known name \"org.example.foo\", then you might adjust your snap's yaml "
"to have:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:48
msgid ""
"name: foo\n"
"...\n"
"slots:\n"
"  dbus-svc: # name that is used with 'snap connect' on slots side\n"
"    interface: dbus\n"
"    bus: session\n"
"    name: org.example.foo\n"
"...\n"
"apps:\n"
"  foo:\n"
"    command: ...\n"
"    slots: [ dbus-svc ]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:63
msgid "Consuming snap (plug)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:64
msgid ""
"As a developer, if you want your snap to communicate over D-Bus with another "
"snap via the \"org.example.foo\" D-Bus well-known name on the `session` bus, "
"you might adjust your snap's yaml to have:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:66
msgid ""
"name: bar\n"
"...\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  foo-svc:  # name that is used with 'snap connect' on plugs side\n"
"    bus: session\n"
"    interface: dbus\n"
"    name: org.example.foo\n"
"...\n"
"apps:\n"
"  bar:\n"
"    command: ...\n"
"    plugs:\n"
"    - foo-svc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:83
msgid "System service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:84
msgid ""
"Services may also listen on the D-Bus system bus. Snaps listening on the "
"system bus run as root and may be accessed by any user on the system. While "
"the snapd security policy will limit which connecting snaps can communicate "
"with the service, slot implementations may want to perform additional "
"permission checks (eg, UID) to further limit access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:86
msgid "Providing snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:87
msgid ""
"As a developer, if your application listens on the `system` bus with the "
"well-known name \"org.example.foo\", then the snap's yaml is the same as "
"above, but specify the `system` bus:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:89
msgid ""
"name: foo\n"
"...\n"
"slots:\n"
"  dbus-svc: # name that is used with 'snap connect' on slots side\n"
"    interface: dbus\n"
"    bus: system\n"
"    name: org.example.foo\n"
"...\n"
"apps:\n"
"  foo:\n"
"    command: ...\n"
"    slots: [ dbus-svc ]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:104
msgid "Consuming snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:105
msgid ""
"As a developer, if you want your snap to communicate over D-Bus with another "
"snap via the \"org.example.foo\" D-Bus well-known name on the `system` bus, "
"then the snap's yaml is the same as above, but specify the `system` "
"bus:slight_smile:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:106
msgid ""
"name: bar\n"
"...\n"
"plugs:\n"
"  foo-svc:  # name that is used with 'snap connect' on plugs side\n"
"    bus: system\n"
"    interface: dbus\n"
"    name: org.example.foo\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:117
msgid "Snap dbus interface connections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:119
msgid ""
"As a user, if you want to allow `bar` to communicate with `foo` via D-Bus, "
"then you can connect the interface like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:121
msgid "$ sudo snap connect bar:foo-svc foo:dbus-svc\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:125
msgid "You can check it's worked with the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:127
msgid ""
"$ snap connections\n"
"Interface           Plug                 Slot               Notes\n"
"dbus-svc            bar:dbus-svc         foo:dbus-svc       -\n"
"[...]\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:134
msgid "To disconnect:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/dbus-interface.md:135
msgid "$ sudo snap disconnect bar:foo-svc foo:dbus-svc\n"
msgstr ""
